{"action":"created","issue":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/issues/23540","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/issues/23540/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/issues/23540/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/issues/23540/events","html_url":"https://github.com/numpy/numpy/issues/23540","id":1657690399,"node_id":"I_kwDOAA3dP85izlkf","number":23540,"title":"ENH: ufunc should warn when argument `where` is specified and `out` is default None.","user":{"login":"Game4Move78","id":83040764,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzMDQwNzY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83040764?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Game4Move78","html_url":"https://github.com/Game4Move78","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Game4Move78/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Game4Move78/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Game4Move78/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Game4Move78/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Game4Move78/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Game4Move78/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Game4Move78/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Game4Move78/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Game4Move78/received_events","type":"User","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2023-04-06T16:03:23Z","updated_at":"2023-04-06T17:15:25Z","closed_at":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"body":"### Proposed new feature or change:

My argument is that `where` makes sense unless `out` is default `None`, in which case it simply obscures the creation of a partially uninitialised array.

The casual numpy user accessing through the public API likely only wants garbage values if they have explicitly asked for them using `empty_like`. If they have decided not to provide `out`, it probably means they expect a partially transformed copy of the input array and have overlooked the note in the docstring.

Example:

User creates a function that takes log on values where log is defined .

```python
def safe_log(val, out):
    return np.log(val, where=np.greater(val, 0), out=out)
```

User suddenly decides that they don't want to specify `out` every time, making `safe_log` unsafe.

```python
def safe_log(val, out=None):
    return np.log(val, where=np.greater(val, 0), out=out)
```","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/issues/23540/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/issues/23540/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},"comment":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/issues/comments/1499378260","html_url":"https://github.com/numpy/numpy/issues/23540#issuecomment-1499378260","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/issues/23540","id":1499378260,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAA3dP85ZXrJU","user":{"login":"eric-wieser","id":425260,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNTI2MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/425260?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-wieser","html_url":"https://github.com/eric-wieser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-wieser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-wieser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-wieser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-wieser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-wieser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-wieser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-wieser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-wieser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eric-wieser/received_events","type":"User","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-04-06T17:15:25Z","updated_at":"2023-04-06T17:15:25Z","author_association":"MEMBER","body":"The difficulty in using `empty_like` is that you now have to guess the right return type rather than letting `np.log` pick it for you.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/issues/comments/1499378260/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_